Re-deriving: if \(\min(S)=k\), then \(|S|=k\), so after including \(k\) we choose \(k-1\) more elements from \(\{k+1,\dots,16\}\), giving \(\binom{16-k}{k-1}\). This is nonzero for \(k\le 8\):

\[
\sum_{k=1}^{8}\binom{16-k}{k-1}
= \binom{15}{0}+\binom{14}{1}+\binom{13}{2}+\binom{12}{3}+\binom{11}{4}+\binom{10}{5}+\binom{9}{6}+\binom{8}{7}
\]

\[
=1+14+78+220+330+252+84+8=987.
\]

This matches the known identity that the count equals \(F_{17}=987\). My earlier arithmetic stopped incorrectly at 979 and dropped the final \(+8\); the final stated answer 979 was wrong.

